<article class="env-lemma" id="08Q8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08Q8">Lemma <span data-tag="08Q8">21.39.6</span>.</a> Notation and assumptions as in Example <a href="/tag/08PF" data-tag="08PF">21.39.1</a>. Let $B \to B'$ be a ring map. Consider the commutative diagram of ringed topoi </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}), \underline{B}) \ar[d]_\pi &  (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}), \underline{B'}) \ar[d]^{\pi '} \ar[l]^ h \\  (*, B) &  (*, B') \ar[l]_ f }  \]
</div>
  <p> Then $L\pi _! \circ Lh^* = Lf^* \circ L\pi '_!$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Both functors are right adjoint to the obvious functor $D(B') \to D(\underline{B})$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>